// Microwatt syscon chipset device (CPU_CTRL, which Linux reads for the core
// count and writes to start secondary CPUs), with netlists generated by
// piton/tools/bin/convert_microwatt (syscon, syscon2). Every configuration whose
// devices*.xml lists mw_syscon needs this flist AND --define PITON_MW_SYSCON.
// mw_noc_wb.v comes from Flist.mw_xics, which every syscon configuration also
// lists (Microwatt Linux needs the XICS too).
mw_syscon.v
../gen/mw_syscon_flat.v
../gen/mw_syscon_flat_n2.v
